refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;

 arraynullerror_get_last




 Gets information about the last error that occurred.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns an associative array describing the last error with keys "type", "message", "file" and "line". If the error has been caused by a PHP internal function then the "message" begins with its name. Returns &null; if there hasn't been an error yet.
As of PHP 8.5.0, for fatal errors with fatal_error_backtraces enabled, the array also contains a "trace" key with the backtrace as an array. Fatal errors caused by uncaught exceptions do not include this key.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     The returned array now includes a "trace" key
     when a fatal error backtrace is available.

  &reftitle.examples;



    An error_get_last example


<?php
echo $a;
print_r(error_get_last());
?>


    &example.outputs.similar;


Array
(
    [type] => 8
    [message] => Undefined variable: a
    [file] => C:\WWW\index.php
    [line] => 2
)
